### 2. Breadth-First Search (BFS)
BFS is a more straightforward algorithm that explores the neighbor nodes at the present depth prior to moving on to nodes at the next depth level.

```python
def bfs(graph, start, goal):
    visited, queue = set(), [start]
    while queue:
        vertex = queue.pop(0)
        if vertex not in visited:
            visited.add(vertex)
            if vertex == goal:
                return True
            queue.extend(graph[vertex] - visited)
    return False

